let g:mksk_python = 'python'
let g:mksk_args = ['--port', get(g:, 'LMSH_PORT', 8080)]
let g:mksk_layout = 'right'
"let g:mksk_toggle_key = '<M-m>'
" plan folder = the current directory when mksk starts. Override:
"let g:mksk_dir = '~/echo-home/Documents/mksk'
" plan opened at start = the most up-to-date mksk--<plan>--YYYY-MM-DD.md in the folder, else a zero plan. Override:
"let g:mksk_plan = 'db-migration'


map mksk1 : silent source ~/echo-home/.vim/mimd/mksk/mksk.lua<CR>
map mkski : exec 'Mksk --port '.get(g:, 'LMSH_PORT', 8080)<CR>
map mkskt : MkskToggle<CR>
map mkskd : MkskDiff<CR>
map mkskf : MkskFile<CR>
map mkskj : InetJoin mksk<CR>
map mkskl : InetLeave mksk<CR>
map mkskq : MkskQuit<CR>

"HELP:
"- mksk is the make-sketch planner, cloned from neos: it keeps mksk--<plan_name>--YYYY-MM-DD.md up to date with you
"  (format: ~/echo-home/Documents/specs/make-sketch.md): plan updates and questions, on your request. mksk1 loads and
"  opens it on the most up-to-date plan file in the current directory, else on a zero plan (it names it when the first
"  change is saved). :Mksk <plan> opens a named plan instead (a new name starts a new plan).
"- Recall the chat from anywhere (normal/insert/terminal): Alt-m. In visual mode Alt-m attaches the selected lines
"  (e.g. rows of the targets table: "weigh these").
"- Ask without opening the float: :MkskAsk <text>, or :'<,'>MkskAsk <text> to attach a range.
"- In the float: Enter sends, Up/Down history, Ctrl-X interrupts the LLM, Ctrl-C cancels, F2 raw LLM log, F8 network pane,
"  q hides. Busy: plain text steers the running request, !text steers now, +text queues a new request.
"- Float position: Alt-h/j/k/l docks it left/bottom/top/right, Alt-c center, Alt-f full, Alt-b peek (translucent;
"  needs termguicolors). :MkskLayout <name> or g:mksk_layout picks one.
"- Nothing is written without you: edits are staged and shown as a diff. y applies, n drops, v opens saved | proposed side
"  by side (mkskd any time), any other text tells it what to change. Approved changes always go to today's file (the
"  first one of a day creates it from the newest); older files are never written. Suggestions: pick numbers (1,3), all,
"  none, w (skip them and go straight to the diff of what is staged), or answer in your own words; Enter on an option
"  line picks it.
"- Memory: the whole chat stays in its context from start to quit (mkskq); ===r forgets it. ===s shows where the plan stands.
"- Intelligence Network: task assignment exists only once mksk joins it. mkskj joins echo-net as @mksk (name/purpose:
"  g:inet_agents.mksk in vimpage_inet, optional). Then "assign dump_restore to memphia" records the agent and sends it
"  the target's brief, after your y.
"  Progress agents report to @mksk is staged and queued; ===p reviews the queue (y/n each). The network never writes the file.
"- The plan functions are plain Lua (mksk_plan.lua): :lua require('mksk').plan.edit_target{target='cutover', status='WIP'}
"  then :MkskDiff and :lua require('mksk').plan.commit()  (or .discard()).
